    "summary": "After Namdhari raids on Malodh and Malerkotla, Deputy Commissioner J. L. Cowan of Ludhiana had captured Kukas blown from guns on the Malerkotla parade ground. It was a colonial execution as massacre: forty-nine without trial on 17 January 1872, a fiftieth cut down, sixteen more the next day under Commissioner Forsyth. The Under-Secretary told the Commons Cowan had held no trial of any sort. The Government of India dismissed him.",
